{#-
  BLOCK: grid — the wrappers that place gallery listings on the page.

  `rows`: a single column of `gallery:row` listings, each already a `<tr>`.
  `cards`: Design's two-across gallery, 264px cards with a 16px gutter. A short
  last row keeps its empty cell: a `<tr>` with fewer `<td>`s than its siblings
  collapses the column widths in Outlook.

  `tr-stack` on the card cells is B4 and is load-bearing: it stacks the two
  columns on a phone, and the gutter cell carries `tr-hide` so it goes too.
-#}
{% if shape == 'rows' -%}
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:0 28px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;">{{ cards | join('') }}</table></td></tr>
{%- elif shape == 'cards' -%}
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:0 28px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;">
            {%- for row in rows %}<tr><td class="tr-stack" width="50%" valign="top" style="padding:14px 0;">{{ row[0] }}</td><td class="tr-hide" width="16" style="width:16px;"></td><td class="tr-stack" width="50%" valign="top" style="padding:14px 0;">{{ row[1] }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
          </table></td></tr>
{%- endif %}
